# Reduce `r_/` (B6): a right fold along the leading axis, as in J, BQN
# and APL: `'- r_/ 1 2 3` is 1 - (2 - 3). A matrix folds its rows item
# by item; a scalar is a one-item vector. Any function value may be the
# operand: a symbol, a named built-in, a lambda or a user function.
# The grouping shows: the largest Int plus (1 + -1) does not overflow.
# Curried without its array, reduce names a function (`u:s_um`).
== SOURCE
'+ r_/ 1 2 3 4
'- r_/ 1 2 3
'{ (10 * _l) + _r } r_/ 1 2 3
'm_ax r_/ 3 1 4 1 5
'+ r_/ 2 3 r_eshape r_ange 6
'+ r_/ 7
u:m_ul := { a b -> a * b }
'u:m_ul r_/ 1 2 3 4
'& r_/ 1 1 0
'+ r_/ 0.5 0.25
'+ r_/ 9223372036854775807 1 -1
u:s_um := r_/ '+
u:s_um 1 2 3 4
